Assertions:
[STATUS] Both PUT requests return 2xx {SPEC}
[MATH] After the first PUT tags.length = 1 and the single entry equals the group name that was sent {SPEC}
[MATH] After the clearing PUT tags.length = 0 - an empty collection is a real removal, not a rejected no-op {SPEC}
[API] The baseline read and the final read agree, so the case leaves the entity as it found it {OBSERVED}

[MATH] Untagged state: direct = 0 and inherited = 0 {SPEC}
[MATH] Direct-only state: direct = 1 and inherited = 0 {SPEC}
[MATH] Inherited-only state: direct = 0 and inherited = 1 - the parent's grant is counted on the child, once {SPEC}
[MATH] Mixed state: direct = 1 and inherited = 1, so the two groups are never collapsed into one figure {SPEC}

[API] The product's own tags collection stays EMPTY - inheritance never writes a tag onto the descendant {SPEC}
[MATH] The product's inheritedTags.length = 1 and its entry equals the group put on the category {SPEC}
[MATH] After the category tag is cleared the product's inheritedTags.length = 0 {SPEC}
[API] The setting read in the SETUP step is DownTree; under UpTree a product computes no inherited tags and this case must be reported as not applicable rather than failed {SPEC}

[MATH] midCategory inheritedTags.length = 1 {SPEC}
[MATH] leafCategory inheritedTags.length = 1 - inheritance does not stop after one level {SPEC}
[MATH] leafProduct inheritedTags.length = 1, so the chain reaches a product three levels below the grant {SPEC}
[API] None of the three descendants gained an entry in its OWN tags collection {SPEC}

[MATH] Before the removal childEntity inheritedTags.length = 1 - the precondition of the case is itself asserted, so a vacuous pass is impossible {SPEC}
[MATH] After the removal childEntity inheritedTags.length = 0 {SPEC}
[API] The child's own tags collection is unchanged by both writes - revoking on the parent must not touch a direct grant {SPEC}

[MATH] The product's inheritedTags.length = 1 {SPEC}
[MATH] The variation's inheritedTags.length = 1 - a variation is reached by the same grant as its parent product {SPEC}
[API] The variation carries no entry in its own tags collection {SPEC}

[STATUS] Both search requests return 200 {SPEC}
[API] The groupA result set contains entityA and does NOT contain entityB {SPEC}
[API] The groupB result set contains entityB and does NOT contain entityA - the two filters do not leak into each other {SPEC}
[MATH] Each result set's totalCount = the number of entities this case tagged with that group (1) {SPEC}

[STATUS] The PUT issued without personalization:update returns 401 or 403 {SPEC}
[API] targetProduct's tags collection is byte-for-byte what it was before the attempt - the status alone is not the assertion, because a 2xx that writes nothing and a 403 are different defects {SPEC}
[API] The permission personalization:update is present in GET /api/platform/security/permissions, so the gate is a declared contract rather than an assumption {SPEC}

[API] With EventBasedIndexation false the indexed user_groups value is UNCHANGED immediately after the tag write - the grant is pending, not applied {SPEC}
[API] With EventBasedIndexation true the same read may already carry the new group; the recorded setting decides which of the two expectations applies, and the case reports which branch it took {SPEC}
[API] After the explicit reindex the indexed user_groups carries exactly the assigned group {SPEC}
[API] After the tag is cleared and the entity reindexed, user_groups returns to the default bucket rather than staying on the removed group {SPEC}

[API] controlProduct's tags and inheritedTags are both empty, so it is genuinely unrestricted {SPEC}
[API] Its indexed user_groups carries the default 'any' bucket rather than an empty value - an entity nobody restricted must remain reachable by anonymous shoppers {SPEC}
[MATH] The indexed user_groups collection length = 1 for an untagged entity, so the default is a real value and not an accident of an absent field {SPEC}
